  "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{3}-6}{{x}^{2}-4}=$",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{3}-6}{{x}^{2}-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[2{x}^{3}-6]^{\u2032}}{[{x}^{2}-4]^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }3x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
